{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right","id":1501633,"title":"Nephandic Ascension: Buddhist Monk; What if the Nephandi are right?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-29T12:18:50-08:00","id":1501633,"title":"Nephandic Ascension: Buddhist Monk; What if the Nephandi are right?","content":"So, for many years I have thought about the Nephandic philosophies (dont worry, I haven't sold my soul yet), and one thing that most people agree is that evil for evil's sake is rather silly, except if you some sort of cosmic force that simply cannot avoid it (like gravity).<br /> <br /> In the case of the dreaded Nephandi, the center of their philosophy is <b>Nihilism</b>. The idea that there is no purpose in existance. There's also Hedonism, but that's the consequence of their nihilism rather than a central dogma of their belief system.<br /> <br /> There is, however, one philosophical/religious group in real life that has nihilistic ideas as the main pillar dogma of their doctrines: &quot;orthodox&quot; Buddhism.<br /> <br /> In the buddhism as professed by Siddhartha Gautama, aka the &quot;historic Buddha&quot; (as opposed to many other denominations that came after), existance is suffering, and what's more, it's an eternal cicle of suffering. Life, Death, Reencarnation, and suffering.<br /> <br /> In this view of Buddhism, Gods are ignored. Original Buddhism was &quot;agnostic&quot;, as in, it didnt professed the existence of any Gods, but it didnt rejected them either. Gods were just simply irrelevant for the process of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> By the way, for the original Buddhism, even if God(s) were to be real, they are also trapped in the same cicle of suffering. Even thou living as a God must feel like partying everyday in Paradise, even eternity must come to an end - and when that happens, the Gods will suffer even more than any other being, because they will at least once inevitably have to face Death, and because they are so unprepared for it, it would be an even greater suffering for them.<br /> <br /> The purpose of Buddhism is to become &quot;Enlightened&quot;, and with that, reach Nirvana (I guess I know exactly from where the writers of Mage got the idea of &quot;Ascension&quot;).<br /> <br /> However, people in the West have the wrong idea of what &quot;Nirvana&quot; is, and even other branches of Buddhism distorted the message from Siddhartha Gautama.<br /> <br /> Nirvana is NOT Paradise. Nirvana is cutting oneself from the eternal cicle of life-death-rebirth and suffering. Becoming &quot;Enlightened&quot; means being able to see and recognize the cicle, and then cutting oneself from it.<br /> <br /> In other others: it means DISSOLUTION. The complete dissolution of the Ego into... Nothingness.<br /> <br /> And now, back to our favorite bad guys: the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Now, must Nephandi, consumed by their Nihilism, become utterly Hedonistic.<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <br /> I've made a Buddhist Monk who is a Nephandi. And no, he's not a fake. He's a true adherent to Buddhism. And he's not an Hedonist.<br /> <br /> In fact, he wants to bring the absolute destruction of everything... Out of compassion. To free all existence from the cruel cicle of senseless and purposeless suffering. <br /> <br /> He doesnt torture or torment others or indulge in vices, because what he wants is to truthfully free everybody from the suffering with no purpose that is existing.<br /> <br /> Now, what do you guys think? Is Ascension the final dissolution of the Ego - with is no different from becoming &quot;One with the Universe&quot;. After all, once you become a part of everything, you actually becomes... Nothing. All the parts that made &quot;you&quot; to be you, all that you were is gone.<br /> <br /> Could Ascension be the dissolution of the Self?<br /> <br /> And in that case... Doesnt that mean that the Nephandi were right all along, and are the only truly sane ones?<br /> <br /> Does Ascension and &quot;Descension&quot; meet each other at the final stage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T17:07:23-08:00","id":1501650,"title":"","content":"Firesign Theater was right &quot;Dig a deep enough hole and everyone will want to jump in.&quot; Nihilism doesn't need ritual and sacrifice the Nephandi desperately do. The Nephandi need Nihilism as a mask to cover their selfish appetites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T17:16:14-08:00","id":1501652,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Honestly, the kind of person who would turn Nephandi out of genuine compassion...is one the Caul would instantly destroy. Because they are obviously driven by a capacity that prevents you from embracing the worst aspects of your own negation for power.<br /> <br /> Universal Descent one possible form of the Black Diamond, but really, most Nephandi who even reach the point where they can seriously contemplate their apogee are after the Consummation of Leviathan - the world will still be there, they just get to rule it.<br /> <br /> Still, it is worth considering that Nirvana is, in a sense, voluntary annihilation - the complete loss of illusion there is a self. Something a wise Awakened Buddhist might need to be self-aware of, that the Caul seems like a shortcut - and that leads to hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T20:54:47-08:00","id":1501664,"title":"","content":"So, would you say that the Nephandi are, perhaps, right about the final destination, but wrong about the path?<br /> <br /> Do they too fall short to the measurement and end up trapped the in same web of illusions that both sleepers and awakened are trapped in?<br /> <br /> Also, would the final stage of Ascension, Transcendence, Nirvana or whatever would you wanna call it, be it, self annihilation, the final dissolution? True... Death?<br /> <br /> If it were, then the path of screams of the Nephandi suddenly becomes so much more understandable. I can totally understand surrendering to despair if this is it.<br /> <br /> And, do Nephandi are truly this 1 dimensional? Cant they have anything more in store for them? Are they in it just for power for power's sake in the middle of their despair? Couldnt they however embrace nihilism fully, somewhat like the Spectres from Wraith the Oblivion do, and be more like the Captain of the sinking vessel that has resigned himself to his fate? I mean, sure, I can totally understand that madmen laughing at the world ending and are just in for the fireworks, but cant there be more to it?<br /> <br /> I want to do an exercise on the very nature of evil here, more than just looking at the results of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T21:00:03-08:00","id":1501665,"title":"","content":"So, what you guys are saying is, that the Nephandi may talk big game about undoing this theater of madmen to stop the madness of existing, but in actuality what they truly want is to rule in Hell, is that it? That is also another interesting take, Im not gonna lie. But... It seems off to me. I always saw Nephandi kind like Spectres of the living kind...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T21:26:27-08:00","id":1501666,"title":"","content":"The Nephandi <i>might</i> be right about the final destination, or they might be wrong about that (only those who have Ascended know for sure \u2014 or don't, if the Buddhist idea of Nirvana as you present it is right); but they're <i>very definitely</i> wrong about how to get there.<br /> <br /> And the Nephandi as presented in <b>Book of the Fallen</b> haven't succumbed to despair. The common thread in all of the Paradigms described isnt nihilism; it's sociopathy, with the best of them not caring about the pain they inflict on others and the worst of them actively delighting in it.<br /> <br /> If you want a \u201cheroic\u201d Nephandus, I'd look to shows like Dexter for inspiration: the Nephandus strictly limits who he subjects to his cruelty, and perhaps sees himself as an avenging angel who metes out poetic justice to punish the wicked. As long as he doesn't slip up and punish the wrong person, which is <i>very</i> easy for him to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-30-2023, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T12:26:24-08:00","id":1501736,"title":"","content":"As Dataweaver said, like some Nephandi might have gone made from cosmic despair, but that's not universal, and the core tenant seems to be sociopathy rather than despair, a thing that is not helped by the progression through their personal descent. Just being an 'Evil' mage doesn't make you Nephandi, there are particular things you need to do...and they generally don't 'do' compassion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T05:56:40-08:00","id":1501807,"title":"","content":"Well yes, while being a psychopath is an easy way to understand someone who doesn't care at all about anybody else, that also doesnt mean you are automatically a serial killer.<br /> <br /> I was thinking, back to the Buddhist Monk, he could want to destroy all out of &quot;compassion&quot;... But that could just be the result of being totally devoided of empathy. &quot;Dont be afraid child, Im killing you for your own good... You'll be better this way&quot;. But deep down, he does it without feeling any kind of guilty or remorse - perhaps even enjoying it. Like a true psychopath, meanwhile rationalizing it as &quot;compassion&quot; for himself and others. Would that be possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T06:18:47-08:00","id":1501808,"title":"","content":"It's certainly possible. He might also feel the remorse but for whatever reason feel no need act on it. A lot of Nephandi seem to show real remorse and compassion right up to the point that they slip the knife in. That is usually interpreted to mean that the regret was an act, but it might be quite real but somehow irrelevant. Or it could be real but overwhelmed by an even greater skewed compassion inflicted by his inversion. <br /> <br /> There are lots of possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T07:13:04-08:00","id":1501811,"title":"","content":"Aye, like one could have an <i>excess</i> of empathy towards &quot;the world&quot;, made seem as a sort of weird &quot;compassion&quot;. Involving oneself with the world always has to bring up some karma, which usually leads to pain. Empathy could imply that one <i>suffers </i>the pain of others. Exaggetated to the point where you want to carry &quot;the world&quot; whole suffering over your shoulders (a show of hubris), no wonder it would end bringing up pain.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Inverted Avatar focuses &quot;the pain of the world&quot; over the fallen monk's 5 aggregates, with the intent of making the idea to inflict smaller pains within the &quot;noble&quot; goal to end all of it seem acceptable (&quot;smaller pains&quot; being pretty much anything imaginable, since the world it's always going to be bigger).<br /> <br /> NVM that it's a downward spiral of horror, the mage ultimately inflicting pain, assuming karma, and getting further from any true freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T14:58:05-08:00","id":1501987,"title":"","content":"I feel that you are also horribly misrepresenting what Buddhism is about. Nihilism is not what Buddhism ascribes to, Nihilist values are directly against the moral codes that Siddhartha espoused. Yes, life is suffering, but that does not mean morality and kindness are empty exercises. The goal of Buddhism is to master oneself and avoid excess allowing you to lessen your own karmic burden and the burden you bring upon others. The core tenets are inherently centered on yourself and your conduct towards others.<br /> <br /> Your concept for a specific Nephandi who claims to be a Buddhist and operates like this is valid, but that doesn't mean he is actually acting towards Samsara, he's just got a very complicated explanation for why he is making everyone suffer. Because that's the point of the Nephandi, everyone must suffer because of the Nephandus and his desires.<br /> <br /> Nirvana is supposed to be about losing the illusion of self and shedding the suffering of an endless cycle of rebirth. That might be Ascension, then again it might not. Descension is about being the most selfish and cruel thing in the cosmos. So no, I don't see any way of those two things being the same, except in the mind of a crazed Magus fueled by the &quot;enlightenment&quot; of the Cauls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T17:30:41-08:00","id":1501991,"title":"","content":"This\u2026 makes about as much sense as a Christian Nephandus claiming that suborning all humans\u2019 free will unto Satan is doing God\u2019s work.<br /> <br /> Which is what a Nephandus would say and believe in, but it hardly has to do anything with true Christian faith, unless I\u2019m seriously missing something.<br /> <br /> And I see that Asmodai above already explained it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 02-02-2023, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T08:23:50-08:00","id":1502023,"title":"","content":"Yeah.<br /> <br /> Interestingly &quot;Buddhism it's nihilism&quot; it's a posture that was taken by the <i>opponents </i>of buddhist faith even in India - I think they used to call Buddhists something akin to &quot;worshippers of nothingness&quot;. Nedless to say, this was (and is) slander ... but understandably effective slander<br /> <br /> My limited understanding of these matters it's that the &quot;illusion of the self&quot; doesn't mean as much that that there's &quot;nothing&quot; where you see a self, but rather that there's the <i>aggregates</i>, which are accidental and impermanent, that one perceives as a single entity because they happen to be together - and once you remove all of these stuff, there's &quot;nothing&quot; that subsides as an essence (or soul) that you could call a &quot;you&quot;<br /> <br /> And that, if one wants to compare with an occidental belief, more than with Nihilism this could be compared to the anty-substancialism that one can see on the likes of Hegel or Heidegger","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-03-2023, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T18:56:34-08:00","id":1502267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1501987#post1501987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that you are also horribly misrepresenting what Buddhism is about. Nihilism is not what Buddhism ascribes to, Nihilist values are directly against the moral codes that Siddhartha espoused. Yes, life is suffering, but that does not mean morality and kindness are empty exercises. The goal of Buddhism is to master oneself and avoid excess allowing you to lessen your own karmic burden and the burden you bring upon others. The core tenets are inherently centered on yourself and your conduct towards others.<br /> <br /> Your concept for a specific Nephandi who claims to be a Buddhist and operates like this is valid, but that doesn't mean he is actually acting towards Samsara, he's just got a very complicated explanation for why he is making everyone suffer. Because that's the point of the Nephandi, everyone must suffer because of the Nephandus and his desires.<br /> <br /> Nirvana is supposed to be about losing the illusion of self and shedding the suffering of an endless cycle of rebirth. That might be Ascension, then again it might not. Descension is about being the most selfish and cruel thing in the cosmos. So no, I don't see any way of those two things being the same, except in the mind of a crazed Magus fueled by the &quot;enlightenment&quot; of the Cauls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, absolutely, I was oversimplifying things for easy of understand. Absolutely, compassion is a core precept of Buddhism. <br /> <br /> And that was the idea behind this concept. This is most obviously NOT true Buddhism; this is Descent, after all, so it's obvious that it is a corrupted and skewed view on the Buddhist Enlightment.<br /> <br /> I just wanted something more than just &quot;lets be a holes&quot; and something that could come in an organic way from a deturpation of paths of Enlightment.<br /> <br /> You know, like the cliche tale of &quot;old master with anxious/proud student, student turns evil&quot;, upon which the student believes himself to overcome his master and to have unlocked the secret truths/powers the master kept hidden from him, and &quot;now I see the truth&quot; and whatnot. <br /> <br /> It's a path of damnation brought by pure hubris, and the more the student follows it, the more he lose himself in his corruption. <br /> <br /> Have you ever played &quot;Knights of the Old Republic&quot;? It's an old Star Wars RPG game that details the origin of the Sith, and that for the first time gives the Sith a true philosophical ideology other than just &quot;we be evil&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Jedi are a good example of Buddhist-like fictional group - the inspiration from Buddhism to create them is clearly obvious.<br /> <br /> Their Sith counterpart on the other hand, are different. And the closer thing of their philosophy is the Nietzschean wan, the Ubersmench (the infamous one for reasons we all know), and his idea of &quot;will-to-power&quot; (interestingly, the Dark Lord Sauron from Lord of the Rings is the same critique on Nietzsche).<br /> <br /> Now, instead of this approach, I was thinking on a corrupted and distorted version of a viable path of wisdom, hence the idea of the &quot;zealot Buddhist&quot;.<br /> <br /> By the way, now that I thought... I may have hit a better mark than I initially planned. I'll explain...<br /> <br /> You see, there was a dictator, from Central America I believe, I just dont remember exactly which country...<br /> <br /> Anyway, the guy was a Buddhist and believed in reencarnation. <br /> <br /> He was a maniac (like all dictators), and he said that it was more sinful to kill an ant than a person, because a person will Reencarnate (thus no harm is done), while the ant would done (thus killing it would be a permanent damage).<br /> <br /> See, there goes my Buddhist Nefandi (a version of, not exactly the one I was thinking but hey, there is precedent).<br /> <br /> I just have to search this guy's name","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T19:23:24-08:00","id":1502270,"title":"","content":"I also like the idea that maybe this universe (not our real one, the game universe) is a Lovecraftian horror theater. Hey, maybe there's no Garden of Eden or the Elysium Fields by the end of the rainbow; maybe all there is on the final ladder is a monstrous beast with a mocking laughter waiting to deliver final oblivion and endless madness to the fools that held to false hopes. Who knows? Maybe the Tellurian is a cosmic mockery designed to inflict nedless suffering in its unsuspecting denizens, and there is no ultimate grand purpose after all, it's all just an illusion created to protect the ones living in it from the utter despair that is the truth.<br /> <br /> In this case, maybe the Technocracy is right, and ignorance, TRULY is a blessing. Because false hope is the only thing keeping chaos and madness away, so maybe &quot;amputating&quot; the wonder of the world may be for the best.<br /> <br /> Or maybe, the best way to live this live is the Nefandi way. Maybe it's all just a farse, maybe your moral codes are just a result of your fear and weakness.<br /> <br /> Fear to accept the truth, the truth that there is no purpose in this existance. No overarching meaning for everything, no great plan, no nothing. Just one eternal night awaiting at the end of all things, and even worse of all, it's not even malignant, it's completely indifferent. Because if it even were malignant, it would indicate that your existance held SOME meaning, even an evil one. But not even that.<br /> <br /> And your weakness, because you lack the necessary strenght to accept the truth and fully embrace it, and to let go of all the bonds that keep you tied up; only by having the strenght to let go, will you ever be truly free - free from your useless and senseless morals, free of your empty world connections in this world.<br /> <br /> This world has no purpose and makes no sense, and the only sensible way to live in such a world is without rules.<br /> <br /> Now everybody remember, our reunions are every Saturday from 1 pm to 4:30 pm and from 5 pm to 9 pm, next Saturday we will discuss &quot;your inner Nefandi&quot; and in the next week we will promote readings of the Malleus Nefandorum, and if any of you want to participate to the group excursion to the Caul next month, remember that it's 75 dollars per person and that each one has to bring their own food since there'll be no stops. And next month dont forget that we want each one of you to bring a friend, and tell them that we are recruiting souls!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T19:39:23-08:00","id":1502272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1501991#post1501991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This\u2026 makes about as much sense as a Christian Nephandus claiming that suborning all humans\u2019 free will unto Satan is doing God\u2019s work.<br /> <br /> Which is what a Nephandus would say and believe in, but it hardly has to do anything with true Christian faith, unless I\u2019m seriously missing something.<br /> <br /> And I see that Asmodai above already explained it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he he, actually it's kind of funny that you mentioned this...<br /> <br /> First of all, at the very early centuries of Christianism, we had the Gnostic movement, which was considered a heresy and burned away, boom, gone.<br /> <br /> Their views however... Were mighty interesting.<br /> <br /> They believed this world we live in to be &quot;ordus mondo&quot;, the world to which we were banned in to after the original sin. This is therefore, the world o sin.<br /> <br /> Satan is the master of this world. And that's why there's evil in the world, because we live away from God, we live in sin, and under the reign of Satan.<br /> <br /> Annnnnnnd.... That's why they were purged. You see, if this is the world of Satan, this means that ALL institutions of this world are under the service of the Emperor of this world... And that would include a certain Catholic Apostolic Roman Church...<br /> <br /> Yes, they claimed that the Catholic Church was an institution controlled by the Devil.<br /> <br /> To prove them wrong, the church burned them, so there's that.<br /> <br /> Now, about Satan being doing God's work... You know, that's not exactly a new concept... It's not one that many people adhere to, nor even one that is talked about, but it is not new.<br /> <br /> And Im even kind of sad that you brought that up, because as I was writting the first responses here, I thought &quot;uh, how about I apply the same concept to each one of the Traditions, and create a sort of Dark Mirror Reflections&quot; concept, and obviously I thought about the &quot;lets aid Satan to help achieve God's grand plan&quot; (cliche I know, but it would be just a start), but then I saw your answer and I laughed myself out<br /> <br /> Uh, Im feeling so diabolical today<br /> <br /> PS: about having &quot;something to do with Christianism&quot;, or Buddhism or any other, of course it doesnt have anything to do with those; it's evil Nephandic shit, what did you expect, it's a degenerate, pervasive and corrupted view of the original dogmas, it's a twisted view of concepts distorted by their insanity (or if you're a cruel ST, their views are twisted BY THE TRUTH).<br /> <br /> If those individuals were not messed in their heads, they wouldnt think in those lunatic ways. A Satan servant wouldnt help damn souls to hell if he didnt thought that God is a sadistic tyrant that created humanity to be his playtoys; a crazy Buddhist wouldnt want to destroy the world if he didnt believe that Oblivion is the only ultimate truth. That's the point Im trying to make with this specific kinds and their special brand of Descension.<br /> <br /> Sure, there's still room for the good ol' sadistic psychopath, but Im finding delightful to create those Nephandi with a &quot;purpose&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 02-05-2023, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T03:15:58-08:00","id":1502294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1502272#post1502272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, he he, actually it's kind of funny that you mentioned this...<br /> <br /> First of all, at the very early centuries of Christianism, we had the Gnostic movement, which was considered a heresy and burned away, boom, gone.<br /> <br /> Their views however... Were mighty interesting.<br /> <br /> They believed this world we live in to be &quot;ordus mondo&quot;, the world to which we were banned in to after the original sin. This is therefore, the world o sin.<br /> <br /> Satan is the master of this world. And that's why there's evil in the world, because we live away from God, we live in sin, and under the reign of Satan.<br /> <br /> Annnnnnnd.... That's why they were purged. You see, if this is the world of Satan, this means that ALL institutions of this world are under the service of the Emperor of this world... And that would include a certain Catholic Apostolic Roman Church...<br /> <br /> Yes, they claimed that the Catholic Church was an institution controlled by the Devil.<br /> <br /> To prove them wrong, the church burned them, so there's that.<br /> <br /> Now, about Satan being doing God's work... You know, that's not exactly a new concept... It's not one that many people adhere to, nor even one that is talked about, but it is not new.<br /> <br /> And Im even kind of sad that you brought that up, because as I was writting the first responses here, I thought &quot;uh, how about I apply the same concept to each one of the Traditions, and create a sort of Dark Mirror Reflections&quot; concept, and obviously I thought about the &quot;lets aid Satan to help achieve God's grand plan&quot; (cliche I know, but it would be just a start), but then I saw your answer and I laughed myself out<br /> <br /> Uh, Im feeling so diabolical today<br /> <br /> PS: about having &quot;something to do with Christianism&quot;, or Buddhism or any other, of course it doesnt have anything to do with those; it's evil Nephandic shit, what did you expect, it's a degenerate, pervasive and corrupted view of the original dogmas, it's a twisted view of concepts distorted by their insanity (or if you're a cruel ST, their views are twisted BY THE TRUTH).<br /> <br /> If those individuals were not messed in their heads, they wouldnt think in those lunatic ways. A Satan servant wouldnt help damn souls to hell if he didnt thought that God is a sadistic tyrant that created humanity to be his playtoys; a crazy Buddhist wouldnt want to destroy the world if he didnt believe that Oblivion is the only ultimate truth. That's the point Im trying to make with this specific kinds and their special brand of Descension.<br /> <br /> Sure, there's still room for the good ol' sadistic psychopath, but Im finding delightful to create those Nephandi with a &quot;purpose&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, I fanboy over Mage: The Awakening and the Shin Megami Tensei franchise \u2014 of course I know that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But that wasn\u2019t the particulars of this specific topic, now, was it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T06:20:02-08:00","id":1502300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1502272#post1502272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, he he, actually it's kind of funny that you mentioned this...<br /> <br /> First of all, at the very early centuries of Christianism, we had the Gnostic movement, which was considered a heresy and burned away, boom, gone.<br /> <br /> Their views however... Were mighty interesting.<br /> <br /> They believed this world we live in to be &quot;ordus mondo&quot;, the world to which we were banned in to after the original sin. This is therefore, the world o sin.<br /> <br /> Satan is the master of this world. And that's why there's evil in the world, because we live away from God, we live in sin, and under the reign of Satan.<br /> <br /> Annnnnnnd.... That's why they were purged. You see, if this is the world of Satan, this means that ALL institutions of this world are under the service of the Emperor of this world... And that would include a certain Catholic Apostolic Roman Church...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might be thinking of the Albigensians.<br /> <br /> The Gnostics were a pre-Christian group with a tendency for borrowing imagery and names from existing religions. Some branches of gnosticism (there were quite a few) did profess that the material was evil and the spiritual good. However, the Gnostics were largely on the way out by 250, well before the Church was in a position to persecute anyone (or could be called Roman for that matter).<br /> <br /> The Albigensians were a heretical Christian sect (or extra-Christian religion, depending on who you talk to) from 12th century France. They professed the physical to be entirely evil and in so doing denied a number of core Christian beliefs such as the incarnation of Christ and the resurrection of the body. They also thought sex and marriage were evil (Marriage is a sacrament in the Catholic Church) and suicide was good.<br /> <br /> They were indeed declared heretics and excommunicated, more because of the aforementioned denials of doctrine than anything they said about the Church itself. They were also persecuted, though that was driven as much by the political ambitions of the French and English nobility (see Land Snatching) as any desire to combat heresy. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All that aside, the Albigensian idea that the physical world is fundamentally evil (and especially their alleged promulgation of suicide as a right and proper means to escape it) could also work as a Nephandic motivation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T06:35:32-08:00","id":1502301,"title":"","content":"The Bible also mentions an early heresy built around the notion that God forgives sins, and the more sins you commit the more forgiveness you'll receive; so sinning should be treated as a positive good. It tended to lean more towards hedonism than murder; so it's not <i>really </i>a Nephandic thing. But it <i>does </i>show how easily the basic tenets of a faith can be turned on their head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T09:11:37-08:00","id":1502309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1502300#post1502300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you might be thinking of the Albigensians.<br /> <br /> The Gnostics were a pre-Christian group with a tendency for borrowing imagery and names from existing religions. Some branches of gnosticism (there were quite a few) did profess that the material was evil and the spiritual good. However, the Gnostics were largely on the way out by 250, well before the Church was in a position to persecute anyone (or could be called Roman for that matter).<br /> <br /> The Albigensians were a heretical Christian sect (or extra-Christian religion, depending on who you talk to) from 12th century France. They professed the physical to be entirely evil and in so doing denied a number of core Christian beliefs such as the incarnation of Christ and the resurrection of the body. They also thought sex and marriage were evil (Marriage is a sacrament in the Catholic Church) and suicide was good.<br /> <br /> They were indeed declared heretics and excommunicated, more because of the aforementioned denials of doctrine than anything they said about the Church itself. They were also persecuted, though that was driven as much by the political ambitions of the French and English nobility (see Land Snatching) as any desire to combat heresy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All that aside, the Albigensian idea that the physical world is fundamentally evil (and especially their alleged promulgation of suicide as a right and proper means to escape it) could also work as a Nephandic motivation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's exactly it, thank you very much. I had seing a documentary about it long time ago, I remember it were from southern France but didnt remember the details, and yes I mixed it with the Gnostics. Thanks for the details.<br /> <br /> And yes, I fully agree, those nutsies would be an awesome mold for building &quot;Nephandic Christians&quot;. In fact, not too distant from my &quot;Buddhist Monk&quot; guy - destroy everything because everything is evil, only Oblivion is a representation of the ultimate good - that's some sick and feasible Nephandic ideology.<br /> <br /> Thanks a lot for the information<br /> <br /> EDIT: and that incentive to suicide, that's some perfectly Nephandic thing<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1502301#post1502301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bible also mentions an early heresy built around the notion that God forgives sins, and the more sins you commit the more forgiveness you'll receive; so sinning should be treated as a positive good. It tended to lean more towards hedonism than murder; so it's not <i>really </i>a Nephandic thing. But it <i>does </i>show how easily the basic tenets of a faith can be turned on their head.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bFunny that you said that, I remember from High School in my literature class about a Portuguese poet (Im brazilian, so we study portuguese-brazilian literature) that was a massive hedonistic person, a poet from medieval time, I dont remember who he was, I'd have to search, but he had this exact reasoning, saying that God loves sin because God loves to forgive sin, and that's why he sinned constantly, so that he could please the lord by being forgiven.<br /> <br /> I still remember one of his poems (in portuguese obviously) where he basically says that young women should... Well, you know... While they are young and beautiful, and that they should do it as much as possible while they can, before age robs them of their beauty. And allegedly he did that poem for a specific woman, a sort of &quot;comon lady, open your legs to me while you're still young&quot;, which it must've been absolutely scandalous at the time.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it is possible to spin our heads and find justifications for one that sells &quot;souls to Satan&quot; in order to &quot;please the Lord&quot;, under very sick and twisted viewpoints (which is exactly what I would want from a Nephandus).<br /> <br /> Another example, for a &quot;generic&quot; Dreamspeaker, so lets assume it's some sort of Animistic/Totemistic religions, and under those the Father Wolf or Bear or the Great Serpent or whatever arent just wild beasts, but rather concious agents that are part of a Natural Order (Im speaking on very broad and generic terms here).<br /> <br /> A Nephandus Dreamspeaker on the other hand may just have a sort of &quot;Darwinian&quot; worldview, however. Thus, instead of seeing Father Wolf as a cog on the &quot;cosmic order&quot;, upon which one of us have a part to play, the Nephandus see no overarching order, but rather a pure naturalistic fight for survival. There's no great scheme over things, just an eternal fight for survival upon which the strong trample over the weak, and the strong survive and the weak perish, thus all morality is a facade that the weak use to hide under.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Funny consideration here... All the &quot;atheistic&quot; propositions are more &quot;Nephandic-like&quot;. Nietzschean and Darwinian ideas, fitting like a glove for Nephandic ideologies... That's an interesting observation coming from an atheist myself...<br /> <br /> (Well, maybe it's not an accident that both were ostensibly used by the Nazis in very twisted ways unintended by the authors)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 02-06-2023, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-28T01:40:53-07:00","id":1559655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right#post1501633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for many years I have thought about the Nephandic philosophies (dont worry, I haven't sold my soul yet), and one thing that most people agree is that evil for evil's sake is rather silly, except if you some sort of cosmic force that simply cannot avoid it (like gravity).</div> </div> </div> </div>If the concept of somebody being purely, objectively evil purely for the sake of being evil is silly, then the opposite must also hold true.<br /> <br /> A being who is meant to represent absolute goodness, free of any temptations, corruption or sin is also just as silly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> In order for good to exist, there must also be evil to provide contrast. Without contrast, we would have no framework by which to recognize and define what good is.<br /> <br /> Also, you make the fatal mistake of judging their motivations from a limited Sleeper's perspective.<br /> <br /> The Awakened operate on a completely different level of cosmic awareness from ordinary mortals. With their ultimate long term goal being to achieve some version of apotheosis and transform into godlike figures. Even the Nephandi pursue this goal to some degree, though they do so by advancing down an inverted Tree of Wisdom, that supposedly culminates in them transforming into a malevolent god.<br /> <br /> <br /> Contrary to what some players might tell you, not all Nephandi are dead set on reducing existence back to a state of absolute nothingness and then fading into oblivion. Some of the Nephandi are seeking to create a new world to replace the current one, which shall be remade in accordance with their own twisted desires. That is very different from the concept of Buddhism trying to escape the cycle. Because the Nephandi are seeking to make the cycle even worse than it already is!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-28T06:58:31-07:00","id":1559658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559655#post1559655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the concept of somebody being purely, objectively evil purely for the sake of being evil is silly, then the opposite must also hold true.<br /> <br /> A being who is meant to represent absolute goodness, free of any temptations, corruption or sin is also just as silly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> In order for good to exist, there must also be evil to provide contrast. Without contrast, we would have no framework by which to recognize and define what good is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are presupposing dualism, in particular the kind of dualism where Good and Evil are equal and opposite powers. That's not at all certain and it is also not the framework being used when people say evil for evil's sake is silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, you make the fatal mistake of judging their motivations from a limited Sleeper's perspective.<br /> <br /> The Awakened operate on a completely different level of cosmic awareness from ordinary mortals. With their ultimate long term goal being to achieve some version of apotheosis and transform into godlike figures. Even the Nephandi pursue this goal to some degree, though they do so by advancing down an inverted Tree of Wisdom, that supposedly culminates in them transforming into a malevolent god. </div> </div> </div>That's certainly a viewpoints some mages take or fall into, but it's not at all what most mages are trying to accomplish, at least not in any intentional way. It might be what their Avatars are trying to get them to do, but that's not the same thing. And if we are going to go down the path of what their Avatars are trying to get them to do, we'd also have to look at what the Nephandi's Avatars are trying to get them to do.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-28T11:40:45-07:00","id":1559659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559658#post1559658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are presupposing dualism, in particular the kind of dualism where Good and Evil are equal and opposite powers. That's not at all certain and it is also not the framework being used when people say evil for evil's sake is silly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it? If it's possible to cut yourself off from the physical world and achieve a state of spiritual perfection, then it seems reasonable to believe the opposite can also be true. A state where instead of rejecting the world's flaws, you decide to wholly embrace them.<br /> <br /> You don't &quot;become one with the universe&quot; by only accepting the best parts of it. You have to accept the darker side too.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am by no means an expert on theology, but I've heard that there are some sects within Buddhist / Hindu practices who follow this very dogma. In their pursuit of enlightenment, they believe that they need to embrace EVERYTHING about the universe, including its darker aspects.<br /> <br /> They paint themselves in ashes, adorn themselves in human bones, and even go so far as to consume feces. All in the attempt to break down and erase their biases.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Supposedly, Dhalsim from the Street Fighter series was actually based on one of these sects, with his necklace being made from the skulls of human children.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-28T12:32:30-07:00","id":1559660,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't &quot;become one with the universe&quot; by only accepting the best parts of it. You have to accept the darker side too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically people that believe things like this aren't &quot;dualistc&quot;, nor &quot;evil&quot; in that essentialist sense. Like: on occident doing human sacrifices it's bad, but sacrificing yourself for your country it's seen as a heroic deed. The action of &quot;sacrifice&quot; isn't <i>essentially </i>good or bad, but rather can be dark or luminous depending on it's relationship with the rest of the &quot;universe&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They paint themselves in ashes, adorn themselves in human bones, and even go so far as to consume feces. All in the attempt to break down and erase their biases. </div> </div> </div>You mean the Aghori? . They do exist on Mage (and I've been told they're a wildly minsunderstood caricature). They aren't Nephandi, tho, they are Extatics.<br /> <br /> That these guys aren't Nephandi, should tell you one or two things about about Nephandi and their special Avatars. They're not about &quot;accepting the dark side&quot;<br /> <br /> You can be very much a &quot;left hand path&quot; mage w/o being a Nephandi. All being <i>a true, Inverted Avatar, Nephandi </i>adds to these concepts it's eliminating the agency of the mage, that now it's forced to follow the path of Descencion for all eternity even after death, and regardless of what beliefs or goals they may have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-28-2026, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-28T14:53:49-07:00","id":1559661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559660#post1559660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean the Aghori? . They do exist on Mage (and I've been told they're a wildly minsunderstood caricature). They aren't Nephandi, tho, they are Extatics.<br /> <br /> That these guys aren't Nephandi, should tell you one or two things about about Nephandi and their special Avatars. They're not about &quot;accepting the dark side&quot;<br /> <br /> You can be very much a &quot;left hand path&quot; mage w/o being a Nephandi. All being <i>a true, Inverted Avatar, Nephandi </i>adds to these concepts it's eliminating the agency of the mage, that now it's forced to follow the path of Descencion for all eternity even after death, and regardless of what beliefs or goals they may have.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, no, I wasn't trying to accuse them of being Nephandi, if it came off that way.<br /> <br /> I was just using them to set a logical precedent that the search for enlightenment isn't necessarily a clean or pretty endeavor.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Nephandi who seek to become dark gods may be the most inhumane creatures in the cosmology, but an evil god is still a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-29T10:25:54-07:00","id":1559664,"title":"","content":"I believe the Tranquil from Dragon Age shows us what a being who is free from all desire and emotional attachment would properly look like.<br /> <br /> Which is to say they'd be a creature who is utterly devoid of personality, while also being virtually powerless to defend themselves against those with hostile intentions.<br /> <br /> Without desire, you have no motivation to do anything. While without attachment, you have no investment in what's going on around you.<br /> <br /> You're just... existing... waiting for that biological clock to tick down to your inevitable demise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-29T12:55:41-07:00","id":1559665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559659#post1559659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't it? If it's possible to cut yourself off from the physical world and achieve a state of spiritual perfection, then it seems reasonable to believe the opposite can also be true. A state where instead of rejecting the world's flaws, you decide to wholly embrace them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if you are asking 'Isn't dualism certain?' or 'Isn't dualism the framework used to say evil for evil's sake is silly?' Or something else. <br /> <br /> You also seem to sometimes assume a form of 'physical = bad, spirit = good' dualism, but not always. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-29T15:11:51-07:00","id":1559666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559665#post1559665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure if you are asking 'Isn't dualism certain?' or 'Isn't dualism the framework used to say evil for evil's sake is silly?' Or something else.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that if people find somebody who is just fundamentally, objectively, absolutely evil is an absurd notion, then the idea of somebody being pure, absolute, divine goodness should also be just as absurd.<br /> <br /> The last time I checked, we were humans; not golden retrievers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559665#post1559665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You also seem to sometimes assume a form of 'physical = bad, spirit = good' dualism, but not always.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's kind of the whole concept behind the Demiurge, is it not?<br /> <br /> The physical world is inherently evil, and so is its creator, while everything that is good exists in the spirit world?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559665#post1559665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> sometimes - but not always.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of how it goes with WoD, due to the unreliable narrator presentation.<br /> <br /> We don't know what do believe anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 04-29-2026, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-30T00:49:11-07:00","id":1559674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559666#post1559666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying that if people find somebody who is just fundamentally, objectively, absolutely evil is an absurd notion, then the idea of somebody being pure, absolute, divine goodness should also be just as absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've misunderstood the point being made. &quot;Evil for evil's sake&quot; isn't a theological or philosophical point, it's about narrative and character motivation.<br /> <br /> The point is that it's easy to have antagonists in stories act in a way that doesn't actually make sense. Character do evil, because they're the antagonist, not because that character has any actual motivations to be evil. That's not to say that it's impossible to do well, but it's quite easy to come across as just bad writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-30T01:30:37-07:00","id":1559675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559674#post1559674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've misunderstood the point being made. &quot;Evil for evil's sake&quot; isn't a theological or philosophical point, it's about narrative and character motivation.<br /> <br /> The point is that it's easy to have antagonists in stories act in a way that doesn't actually make sense. Character do evil, because they're the antagonist, not because that character has any actual motivations to be evil. That's not to say that it's impossible to do well, but it's quite easy to come across as just bad writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe there's a song that covers this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tWYCS6k1IOA\" data-code=\"tWYCS6k1IOA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tWYCS6k1IOA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-30T09:13:52-07:00","id":1559679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559666#post1559666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, that's kind of the whole concept behind the Demiurge, is it not?<br /> The physical world is inherently evil, and so is its creator, while everything that is good exists in the spirit world?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> would enjoy this. Gnosticism was a favorite topic of theirs. It's not all that widespread, though, despite having a disproportionate presence in fiction and movies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm saying that if people find somebody who is just fundamentally, objectively, absolutely evil is an absurd notion, then the idea of somebody being pure, absolute, divine goodness should also be just as absurd. </div> </div> </div>In an equal and opposite form of dualism, yes, in other frameworks no. For example, one common framework is that evil is the rejection of good, making evil lesser. There's also the idea that every action a person takes is for the purpose of bringing about or attaining some perceived good. In either of those (there's significant overlap between the two) evil for evil's sake make's considerably less sense than good for good's sake.<br /> <br /> And as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> points out, it's also not a good fit for storytelling as it doesn't give clear or understandable character motivations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-30T10:04:04-07:00","id":1559681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1502267#post1502267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see, there was a dictator, from Central America I believe, I just dont remember exactly which country...<br /> <br /> Anyway, the guy was a Buddhist and believed in reencarnation.<br /> <br /> He was a maniac (like all dictators), and he said that it was more sinful to kill an ant than a person, because a person will Reencarnate (thus no harm is done), while the ant would done (thus killing it would be a permanent damage).<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I just have to search this guy's name</div> </div> </div> </div>You are likely thinking of either Ne Win or Than Shwe, both from Myanmar. That's South East Asia, and they were mostly influenced by superstition and astrology. The country has a lot Buddist population and backdrop.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Pol Pot (Cambodia), same background in the country but he was explicitly atheist or at least areligious.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-01T09:44:50-07:00","id":1559689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559679#post1559679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> would enjoy this. Gnosticism was a favorite topic of theirs. It's not all that widespread, though, despite having a disproportionate presence in fiction and movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, I thought there were a few Paths, and Roads that followed Gnostic beliefs?<br /> <br /> Cathars being the most immediate example that comes to mind.<br /> <br /> And while it takes place in a completely different setting, I believe the Mastigos also follow it to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-01T11:50:29-07:00","id":1559692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559689#post1559689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, I thought there were a few Paths, and Roads that followed Gnostic beliefs?<br /> <br /> Cathars being the most immediate example that comes to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> ' point is about actual gnostic belief.<br /> <br /> Basically as you point out, lots of modern fiction (including World of Darkness) finds the very harsh version of Gnostic belief fascinating. However it's not historically all that popular. Like, even the original Gnostics tended to be a bit more ambivalent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And while it takes place in a completely different setting, I believe the Mastigos also follow it to some degree. </div> </div> </div>All the mages in Awakening follow this to a degree. That's why they call the world, the <i>Fallen </i>World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-01T14:49:48-07:00","id":1559696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559692#post1559692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All the mages in Awakening follow this to a degree. That's why they call the world, the <i>Fallen </i>World.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. But thanks for clarifying, anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T21:04:13-07:00","id":1561334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1559675#post1559675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there's a song that covers this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of a purely evil character? Yes. Also the silliness of the concept, as he moves from deed to deed without reason or rhyme, at one point stabbing people, at another pushing the elderly and putting pebbles in shoes.<br /> <br /> And yet wouldn't be a Nefandus.<br /> <br /> What makes a Nefandus is the lack of agency on the matter. A Nefandus can't turn back. And that's not in the sense of being punished, but in actual impossibility.<br /> <br /> Nefandi are fated to Descension. The Inverted Avatar isn't just a companion, it interferes far more than a normal one. It strips the Nefandus of everything that constitutes real free will. The Nefandus may think they're in control, but they never are. They're fighting for the obliteration of the universe not because they want, but regardless of what they want.<br /> <br /> It's why they are seem as opposite to a regular Mage. Magic is the realization of one's Will. The powers of the Nefandi, while mechanically identical, are metaphysically the realization of oblivion itself, using the Nefandus as a conduit for it. If a Nefandus even tries to redeem themselves, they'll fight their own psyche, their Avatar and their very power, because that's no Magic that they can control. It's not their belief.<br /> <br /> You can have a character that's utterly evil and they won't be a Nefandus. The Traditions allow slavery and indiscriminate murder of Sleepers after all, you can do a lot of shit without being even formally reprimanded (though others may take matters in their own hands). Everything a Nefandus does, a perfectly normal Mage can do too without risking becoming one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T22:13:03-07:00","id":1561337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1561334#post1561334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nefandi are fated to Descension. The Inverted Avatar isn't just a companion, it interferes far more than a normal one. It strips the Nefandus of everything that constitutes real free will. The Nefandus may think they're in control, but they never are. They're fighting for the obliteration of the universe not because they want, but regardless of what they want.<br /> <br /> It's why they are seem as opposite to a regular Mage. Magic is the realization of one's Will. The powers of the Nefandi, while mechanically identical, are metaphysically the realization of oblivion itself, using the Nefandus as a conduit for it. If a Nefandus even tries to redeem themselves, they'll fight their own psyche, their Avatar and their very power, because that's no Magic that they can control. It's not their belief.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except that we know a Nephandi can not be forced to enter a Caul against their will. Doing so results in their death, every time.<br /> <br /> The mage has to make the conscious and deliberate choice to step through that hell gate. They also have to freely and willfully pledge themselves to the forces of evil.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi was not tricked. It was not coerced into signing some contract.<br /> <br /> They did it of their own volition, actively choosing to become the physical embodiment of entropic evil.<br /> <br /> They could have backed out at any time, right up until the final moment. But still, they chose to press ahead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Tell me, is it slavery when you get what you want!?&quot;</i> - Majin Vegeta.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <br /> I still remain unconvinced that the Nephandi are hard locked into erasing reality, no matter what the books say. Because actions speak louder than words, and in terms of action, only one group of Nephandi are wholly dedicated to that goal, and they are presented as a <b>sub-faction.</b><br /> <br /> Every other Nephandi is presented as being motivated by something else besides just mindless oblivion.<br /> <br /> Can't really call it resisting their evil nature, when nearly all Nephandi have chosen to do exactly that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 07-05-2026, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T01:47:49-07:00","id":1561376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1561337#post1561337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still remain unconvinced that the Nephandi are hard locked into erasing reality</div> </div> </div> </div>That's literally what defines them.<br /> <br /> Everything else about them, any Mage can do without becoming a Nefandus.<br /> <br /> You're focused on what they <i>think</i> and ignoring what they <i>are</i>.<br /> <br /> 1. The Mage doesn't need to understand what being a Nefandus entails to enter a Caul. They have to have <i>some</i> idea, but far from the real full picture.<br /> <br /> 2. It's irreversible. They're not a Nefandus before entering the Caul. Once they do, there's no turning back. Arguing the relevance of that single choice won't change that the thing they become have no further choice.<br /> <br /> 3. Not all Nefandi enter a Caul, there's the Widderslainte, the reincarnated Nefandi. They are born like that and at the same time that can grow up wanting to be a good person (though most don't have enough self to wish that), are simply systematically incapable of accomplishing it.<br /> <br /> 4. Oblivion isn't their <i>goal</i>, it's their <i>function</i>, this is an important distinction. Nefandi can believe whatever and be motivated by whatever. Being one means bringing erasure by nature, not by intention.<br /> <br /> Again, that's their very <i>definition</i>. You can play a Mage that's utterly and irredeemably evil all you want (and a group accepts), that Mage will be a regular Mage that happens to be utterly and irredeemably evil. Not a Nefandus, though maybe at risk of becoming one if tempted with power without full disclosure of the fine print.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T11:31:07-07:00","id":1561392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1561334#post1561334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can have a character that's utterly evil and they won't be a Nefandus. The Traditions allow slavery and indiscriminate murder of Sleepers after all, you can do a lot of shit without being even formally reprimanded (though others may take matters in their own hands).</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't that violate the Tradition Protocols?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T22:09:06-07:00","id":1561410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1561392#post1561392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't that violate the Tradition Protocols?</div> </div> </div> </div>No rule says you can't be a criminal against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T07:25:44-07:00","id":1561417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1561410#post1561410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No rule says you can't be a criminal against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's still different than &quot;the Traditions allow this.&quot; You better get ready for the Oathbreaker Brand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T13:11:19-07:00","id":1561427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1561417#post1561417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but that's still different than &quot;the Traditions allow this.&quot; You better get ready for the Oathbreaker Brand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps not <i>that </i>because, as said, Traditions are not explicit about this. So you're not breaking any oath unless your specific Tradition has a rule against this.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it depends on how solid are your excuses, and on how many powerful mages you can sway, vs how many are appalled by your actions (the victims have no say)<br /> <br /> *There's no rule that says &quot;protect the sleepers&quot;, exept the one about breaking the Veil - and that's not what the rule it's about. I would say the &quot;spirit of the Traditions&quot; it's that you should do this, but since it isn't explicit, and there are explicit rules about protecting mages and ascencion, it's a complicated slippery slope where you can really do a lot if it's &quot;for magick&quot;.<br /> <br /> *And the word of mages it's heavier than even material proof at the tribunals. And the word of powerful mages it's heavier than the word of weaker mages. So sleepers can't do anything about this, their only hope for justice it's that a poweful enough mage cares about this.<br /> <br /> A case in point it's how things like the rape &amp; torture clubs of the Cultists were allowed to exist for years (to awaken people!) 'til <i>another</i> faction finaly managed to get them Barabbi-ed <hr /><br /> It's a good thing to remember that the main villan of Mage, and a total edgelord that's almost cartoonish in his evil, the <i>Grand Harvester of Souls</i> - he ain't a Nephandi. He's a <i>Rogue</i><br /> <br /> And Voormass was on the Traditions for centuries before having to go. He had a whole faction doing unspeakable evil under the nose of the oh-so-virtuous Euthanatos (you know, the guys that believe themselves jury, judge and executioner of bad guys) since, what?, WW2?, before a series of unfortunate events favoring some good mages that had the help of Porthos brought it to the ligth almost a century latter.<br /> <br /> There's no enough love for rogue and hermit mages in the books, but that's another option for evil mages that are too evil and/or too lazy or weak to just do it within the Traditions, but still don't quite want the end-goal of the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-07-2026, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T02:06:22-07:00","id":1561452,"title":"","content":"Not to say you have to be caught, first, and that's not a small thing against a Mage. Their own power offer many ways to hide or destroy evidence, and the Traditions legal system, mostly geared towards letting people do their thing while it doesn't cause problems, kind of compounds.<br /> <br /> As long as you're not a Nefandus, finding out your crimes can be exceedingly hard in the first place, and watching you isn't a high priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T10:18:55-07:00","id":1562002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1561376#post1561376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's literally what defines them.<br /> <br /> Everything else about them, any Mage can do without becoming a Nefandus.<br /> <br /> You're focused on what they <i>think</i> and ignoring what they <i>are</i>.<br /> <br /> 1. The Mage doesn't need to understand what being a Nefandus entails to enter a Caul. They have to have <i>some</i> idea, but far from the real full picture.<br /> <br /> 2. It's irreversible. They're not a Nefandus before entering the Caul. Once they do, there's no turning back. Arguing the relevance of that single choice won't change that the thing they become have no further choice.<br /> <br /> 3. Not all Nefandi enter a Caul, there's the Widderslainte, the reincarnated Nefandi. They are born like that and at the same time that can grow up wanting to be a good person (though most don't have enough self to wish that), are simply systematically incapable of accomplishing it.<br /> <br /> 4. Oblivion isn't their <i>goal</i>, it's their <i>function</i>, this is an important distinction. Nefandi can believe whatever and be motivated by whatever. Being one means bringing erasure by nature, not by intention.<br /> <br /> Again, that's their very <i>definition</i>. You can play a Mage that's utterly and irredeemably evil all you want (and a group accepts), that Mage will be a regular Mage that happens to be utterly and irredeemably evil. Not a Nefandus, though maybe at risk of becoming one if tempted with power without full disclosure of the fine print.</div> </div> </div> </div> I fully agree 101%. A Nephandus, once stepping out of a Caul, becomes a piece of Oblivion itself, and no redemption is possible because they are just a mere conduit to eternal Entropy. The only &quot;redemption&quot; possible would be... Gilgul. That is essentially &quot;spiritual lobotomy&quot;. Largely regarded as worse than death - because it is, the subject left becomes nothing more than a drone.<br /> <br /> Nefandi are like Spectres, except that Spectres from Wraith the Oblivion can still find redemption because they still have a Psyche - probably except for the Malfeans that probably are just past Wraiths Shadows incarnate without any Psyche left. Or like the Fomori from WtA, which is probably an even better correlation; once you become a Fomori, there's no salvation except destruction, that's an incurable &quot;spiritual disease&quot; we could say. It becomes an inseparable part of your being, much like a human can't live without a heart or without a brain or without his lungs.<br /> <br /> And now... We have to talk about the wonders of White Wolf's writing.<br /> <br /> Let's go back to the time of the Second Edition, and to the introductory story of it (that part most everybody ignores or soon forgets).<br /> <br /> Because I remember that one.<br /> <br /> It goes about Senex (yes, the famous Archimage Senex) killing one of his students that becomes a Barabbi. It colourfully describes the raging Nefandus throwing a tantrum at her old master, before she sends her packing towards her next life.<br /> <br /> But then, something funny happens... That same Nefandus avatar reincarnates, you know, just like any other Thursday.<br /> <br /> And the funny thing about this newly born Winderslaint (bah however it is that this weird word is spelled, sorry for it to being wrong).<br /> <br /> But the thing is... She reincarnates into yet another woman that...<br /> ...<br /> ...<br /> ...<br /> <br /> Also becomes an apprentice of Senex.<br /> <br /> The story unfolds with this Mage discovering that her Avatar is... Corrupted. It appears to her as a blood soaked &quot;angel&quot; or something of the sort.<br /> <br /> But here's where things get complicated...<br /> <br /> Because Senex does something to her Avatar that... Not exactly &quot;cures&quot; it, but rather &quot;shields&quot; the mage that owns that Avatar... It shields her from her Nefandus nature.<br /> <br /> So... She basically can operate like any normal Mage and not be affected by the whole &quot;Descent&quot; thing, despite having an &quot;inverted Avatar&quot; due to some occus poccus that Senex did.<br /> <br /> I don't know what to do with that information, and never did I know what to do with it.<br /> <br /> Thoughts anybody? Maybe we should look it up a bit on that little story to refresh the details but yeah... I don't know if that's just some tangent that should be completely ignored, or if it is somehow part of the Mage Canon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T13:09:47-07:00","id":1562003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phooku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1562002#post1562002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nefandi are like Spectres, except that Spectres from Wraith the Oblivion can still find redemption because they still have a Psyche - probably except for the Malfeans that probably are just past Wraiths Shadows incarnate without any Psyche left. Or like the Fomori from WtA, which is probably an even better correlation; once you become a Fomori, there's no salvation except destruction, that's an incurable &quot;spiritual disease&quot; we could say. It becomes an inseparable part of your being, much like a human can't live without a heart or without a brain or without his lungs.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> So... She basically can operate like any normal Mage and not be affected by the whole &quot;Descent&quot; thing, despite having an &quot;inverted Avatar&quot; due to some occus poccus that Senex did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Comparing those entities is complex because they're not quite the same concepts, even if a link does exist.<br /> <br /> A Fomori is contaminated and then fused with a Bane, and that's definitely irreversible. But the &quot;free will&quot; of the resulting entity is up in the air. That's why it's a valid thesis to say that Kindred may be Fomori.<br /> <br /> For them a bigger issue is what mutations the Bane causes, as they may cause mental illness or inhuman hungers. But the lucky ones can be independent and even fight the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> But Nefandus are made into avatars of Oblivion through 4 distinct layers:<br /> <br /> 1. Mental illness, but extreme and with a deep starting point. A Widderslainte is mad since childhood and that won't stop, a Barabi started with the Caul and that's a whole pack to deal with. It can be said their state is more akin to a Quiet, but aligned with absolute nihilism.<br /> <br /> 2. Fate. It's subtle, but life conspires to keep a Nefandus in the path of Descension. It's more visible with a Widderslainte, and includes the eventual finding of other Nefandi.<br /> <br /> 3. The Inverted Avatar. It's not just another flavor of Avatar, the thing is far more intrusive, demanding and wiling to hurt and torture the Nefandus. Even if the person don't think about erasing the universe as a goal, the Avatar does.<br /> <br /> 4. Finally, their &quot;Magic&quot;. Everything a Nefandus do with their spells is tainted with a Nefandic Resonance and starts to corrode reality in the area. The game doesn't goes in length about a mechanic for this, but the overall rules both for Resonance and Paradigm give you all the tools to build fitting answers.<br /> <br /> But the gist of it in short:<br /> <br /> - Nefandus don't follow the rules for Focus or whatever. Their personal belief does not affect their powers.<br /> - Their Instrument is the intent of the Effect, not the execution. Every effect must directly or not contribute to further oblivion.<br /> - Resonance is always intense and uniformly corrupted or destructive. Every single spell will leave this mark, no matter anything else. Some effects in some editions hide this, but nothing erases it.<br /> <br /> And that's it. The individual doesn't matter to how their powers work. They can still believe in a Paradigm of sorts, but it's window dressing, no mechanical requirement or benefit. At most being destructive or perverse helps build the Resonance and set the consequences of the Effect, but the actual execution matters little.<br /> <br /> For the last part, it's hard to tell because it was an early text never referenced again (I never read it, by the way), but you can take as an experiment and imagine what happened from there assuming Senex could only watch and hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T03:42:28-07:00","id":1562077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1562003#post1562003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the last part, it's hard to tell because it was an early text never referenced again (I never read it, by the way), but you can take as an experiment and imagine what happened from there assuming Senex could only watch and hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that one small passage is undoubtedly the type of thing that was a one and done deal and then completely forgotten. I imagine most people don't even know it exists at all.<br /> <br /> It does set up a sort of a precedent thou, even if only for the largely infamous &quot;archspheres&quot;.<br /> <br /> The text does indeed seems to indicate this was some sort of &quot;highly experimental treatment&quot; from the part of Senex. The subject seems to be &quot;healed&quot; - or perhaps, it would be more correct to claim that she's an &quot;asymptomatic carrier of the pathogen&quot;.<br /> <br /> What anyone could do with that information, I leave it to each individual STs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T06:05:20-07:00","id":1562079,"title":"","content":"Precedent? Maybe.<br /> <br /> An experiment isn't necessarily a success. How much was her still capable at Magic after that? For how long? What other effects did she still had?<br /> <br /> The point with the once-and-done story is that its end isn't that much of an end.<br /> <br /> I'd rule out Archspheres. IIRC they don't really go beyond making level 5 effects easier, so it wouldn't so much require one.<br /> <br /> But for all we know, I'd say any remaining capacity to do Magic remains highly dangerous for such a &quot;cured&quot; Widderslainte. Her Avatar is contained, not cured. She's still on Descension, and her Spheres are still Qlippothic. Interesting concept, but I'd still have it sting somehow. Not a failure in the sense of her still going crazy evil and all, but carrying the weight of the touch of that Avatar.<br /> <br /> Still could be a hope, a lifeline and beginning of a process to cleanse the victim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T06:27:17-07:00","id":1562122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501633-nephandic-ascension-buddhist-monk-what-if-the-nephandi-are-right?p=1562079#post1562079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rule out Archspheres. IIRC they don't really go beyond making level 5 effects easier, so it wouldn't so much require one.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that's mostly because there's really isn't much of anywhere to <i>go</i> beyond making level 5 effects easier. As such, my own house rule concerning Archspheres (which I believe is fully in keeping with what official stance there is on them) is that the sixth dot adds all remaining capabilities would make sense for the Sphere that aren't covered by the first five dots. No attempt to itemize them; just a blanket \u201c\u2026and the rest\u201d clause. <br /> <br /> Fixing an Inverted Avatar would be an \u201c\u2026and the rest\u201d for Entropy; so I'd allow it, in theory. <br /> <br /> That said, such Effects are off limits even to Masters for a reason; and as such, even <i>if </i>an Archmaster can pull it off, it doesn't follow that it's ever <i>easy </i>for the Archmaster. And such Effects are likely to be one of a kind things that may not be replicable: just because it was done once (assuming it was), that doesn't mean that it can be done again. Each attempt is a unique effort. <br /> <br /> I agree with your assessment that Senex didn't set a precedent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}